 it at the primary source.\n\n### arXiv:2606.29015 — impartial CGT on the nuclear escalation ladder (→ TODO/1723)#\n\nGenuinely new to the archive: a worked, real-world application of Grundy-value/nim-sum/misère machinery to a staged, ranked process — the archive cites no such precedent. Expected bearing on `1283`: low, argued from the mechanism. The paper's machinery is Nim strategy theory: it answers \"which player holds the winning move\" in adversarial, alternating play. The realm's mechanism consumes only Nim termination theory (well-founded `o<`, decreasing measure); the queue is a one-player cooperative drain with no alternation and no winning condition, and `task_queue_ordinals.md` §7.E already set strategy theory aside for exactly that reason (\"revisit only if an adversarial setting appears\"). --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA101642 - OEIS (https://oeis.org/A101642)\nciteturn1search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 21.8 years ago; Crawled: 1.6 years ago; Jon Asier Bárcena-Petisco, Luis Martínez, María Merino, Juan Manuel Montoya, and Antonio Vera-López, Fibonacci-like partitions and their associated piecewise-defined permutations, arXiv:2503.19696 [math.CO], 2025.\nSmeets】, Mar 20 2024\n\nThe asymptotic density of this sequence is 1/phi^4 = A094214^4 = 0.145898... . - Amiram Eldar, Mar 24 2025\n\nLINKS\n\nA.H.M. Smeets, Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..20000\n\nJon Asier Bárcena-Petisco, Luis Martínez, María Merino, Juan Manuel Montoya, and Antonio Vera-López, Fibonacci-like partitions and their associated piecewise-defined permutations, arXiv:2503.19696 [math.CO], 2025. See p. 5.\n\nW. F. Lunnon, Proof of formula, 2008.\n\nFORMULA\n\nFrom Michel Dekking, Dec 23 2019: (Start)\n\na(n) = 3*A000201(n+1) + 2n - 3.\n\na(n) = A101345(n) + A000201(n+1) + n + 1. (End)\n\nMATHEMATICA\n\nzeck[n_Integer] := Block[{k = Ceiling[ Log[ GoldenRatio, n*Sqrt[5]]], t = n, fr = {}}, While[k > 1, If[t >= Fibonacci[k], AppendTo[ fr, 1]; t = t - Fibonacci[k], AppendTo[fr, 0]]; k-- ]; FromDigits[fr]]; kfp[n_, m_] := Block[{y = Reverse[ IntegerDigits[ zeck[ n]]], z = Reverse[ IntegerDigits[ zeck[ m]]]}, Sum[ y[[i]]*z[[j]]*Fibonacci[i + j + 2], {i, Length[z1]}, {j, Length[z2]}]]; (* Robert G. Wilson v, Feb 04 2005 *)\n\nTable[ kfp[3, n], {n, 50}] (* Robert G. Wilson v, Feb 04 2005 *)\n\nArray[3*Floor[(# + 1)*GoldenRatio] + 2*# - 3 &, 100] (* Paolo Xausa, Mar 23 2024 *)\n\nPROG\n\n(Python)\n\nfrom math import isqrt\n\ndef A101642(n): return 3*(n+1+isqrt(5*(n+1)**2)>>1)+(n<<1)-3 # Chai Wah Wu, Aug 29 2022\n\nCROSSREFS\n\nThird row of array in A101330.\n\nCf. A101345 = Knuth's Fibonacci (or circle) product \"2 o n\".\n\nCf. A000201, A003849, A094214.\n\nKEYWORD\n\nnonn\n\nAUTHOR\n\nN. J. A. Sloane, Jan 26 2005\n\nEXTENSIONS\n\nMore terms from David Applegate, Jan 26 2005\n\nMore terms from Robert G. Wilson v, Feb 04 2005\n\nSTATUS\n\napproved--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ntasks: from research-ingest · jcorbin.tngl.sh/unum@abcf6f3 · Tangled (https://tangled.org/jcorbin.tngl.sh/unum/commit/abcf6f3b462e2a071d3e2f0c769d867e8b51d200)\nciteturn1search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: last month; Sibling tasks: `TODO/1722` (fable analysis of the summary 22 22 + itself), `TODO/1724`, `TODO/1725` (the other two salient sources). 23 23 + related: [1722, 1283, 1286] 24 24 + last_situation: initial 25 25 + reentry_count: 1 26 26 + session_id: 6251cf53-fb9a-43ff-bfa4-8e8d96f19575 27 27 + session_model: opus 28 28 + started_at: \"2026-08-16T21:12:12Z\" 29 29 + session_made_progress: 1 30 30 + last_final_hash: 9f4c85b15f357126 31 31 + no_progress_count: 0 32 32 + last_indicator: done 33 33 + status: done 34 34 + updated_at: \"2026-08-16T21:41:26Z\" 35 35 + --- 36 36 + 37 37 + # 1723 — ingest \"Impartial Combinatorial Games and the Nuclear Escalation Ladder\" 38 38 + 39 39 + Run `skills/research-ingest/SKILL.md`'s procedure against: 40 40 + 41 41 + 